      <title>New Yorkers and Tourists Try to Salvage a Parade Day Postponed by Rain</title>
      <link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/26/nyregion/macys-thanksgiving-day-parade-empty-streets.html</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/26/nyregion/macys-thanksgiving-day-parade-empty-streets.html</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:53:41 +0000</pubDate>
      <enclosure url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/26/multimedia/26met-parade-empty1-vzwf/26met-parade-empty1-vzwf-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg" length="0" type="image/jpeg" />
      <media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/26/multimedia/26met-parade-empty1-vzwf/26met-parade-empty1-vzwf-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg" medium="image" />
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/26/multimedia/26met-parade-empty1-vzwf/26met-parade-empty1-vzwf-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;margin-bottom:10px;" alt="New Yorkers and Tourists Try to Salvage a Parade Day Postponed by Rain" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Wind and rain grounded the beloved balloons that typically dominate the Thanksgiving skies, leaving the streets along the parade route mostly deserted on Thursday.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      <source url="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/26/nyregion/macys-thanksgiving-day-parade-empty-streets.html">The New York Times</source>
